# SABOTAGE: T75 (spec §I2 reply-detection, org-scope pin) — drops the `org_id`
# conjunct from `Samen.Sequences.MailboxReplyCheck.replied_since?/3`'s filter. The
# read is documented as "org-pinned by construction" (the moduledoc's whole point:
# "a reply recorded for a DIFFERENT org's identically-shaped person_id can never
# leak across the boundary") — this patch is exactly that boundary breaking: any
# org's inbound reply for a given `person_id` now pauses EVERY org's enrollment of
# that same `person_id`.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/crm/sequence_send_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: CROSS-ORG: a reply recorded for the SAME person_id under a DIFFERENT org never pauses this org's enrollment
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/sequences/mailbox_reply_check.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/sequences/mailbox_reply_check.ex
index 9d5eeec8..0d121a71 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/sequences/mailbox_reply_check.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/sequences/mailbox_reply_check.ex
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Sequences.MailboxReplyCheck do
         resource
         |> Ash.Query.new()
         |> Ash.Query.filter(
-          org_id == ^org_id and subject_key == "crm.person" and subject_id == ^person_id and
+          subject_key == "crm.person" and subject_id == ^person_id and
             direction == :inbound and ingested_at >= ^cutoff and occurred_at >= ^sent_floor
         )
         |> Ash.Query.limit(1)
